1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
and monsters.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
[theme song playing]

12
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[panting]

13
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[screaming]

14
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
[gasps]

15
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
[panting]

16
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
BAFFLING TURN x OF x EVENTS

17
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Oh, good. You're awake.

18
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Where am I?

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
In a waiting room
that is next to the arena

20
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
for the Final Phase.

21
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
All righty, then.

22
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
[Gon] Oh, right.

23
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I was in the middle of the Hunter Exam.

24
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Your arm will be fine, by the way.

25
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
The break was clean and easily set.

26
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
In fact, that limb will be even stronger

27
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
once it mends.

28
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
In any case,
congratulations on your win, Gon.

29
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
-Mr. Satotz, I--
-You can't.

30
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Just as someone
who has failed the Hunter Exam

31
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
can no longer pass,

32
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
someone who has passed the Hunter Exam

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
can no longer fail.

34
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
What you make of it is entirely up to you.

35
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
If you feel you're unqualified
to be a professional,

36
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
you may put away your license.

37
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Or destroy it, if you wish.

38
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
You can even sell it,

39
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
though it's of no practical use
to anyone else.

40
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
However, you have officially passed
the Hunter Exam,

41
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
and no one who passes it
will ever be allowed to retake it.

42
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Due to the efforts of our predecessors,

43
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
professional Hunters
are treated quite well.

44
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
As a result,

45
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
there is no end of applicants

46
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
seeking a license
for the worst intentions.

47
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
If it weren't for the likes of them,

48
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
we would gladly pass everyone who applies,
without exception.

49
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Most professional Hunters value this card

50
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
even above their own lives.

51
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
All the same,

52
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
it's really nothing more
than a silly piece of junk.

53
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
What's important

54
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
is not the way that you become a Hunter,

55
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
but what you do.

56
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
What I do, huh?

57
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
[Satotz] Gon.

58
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
You must decide for yourself
when you're ready to use this card.

59
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
I'm confident
that you'll make the right choice.

60
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You know,
I got a lot of help to get this far,

61
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
and I owe a lot of people
a bunch of favors.

62
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Once I've paid everyone back,
then I think I'll be ready.

63
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Then please allow me the honor
of congratulating you once again.

64
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Thank you, Mr. Satotz.

65
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
What happened to the other applicants?

66
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
The Exam's still going on, right?

67
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Oh, no. The Exam has already ended.

68
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
-Seriously?
-That's right.

69
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
You've been out for almost the entire day.

70
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[gasps] The entire day?

71
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
The others who passed
are completing a brief orientation,

72
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
the same orientation you'll undergo later.

73
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Who wound up failing?

74
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
It was...

75
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Killua.

76
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
[gasps]

77
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Killua failed?

78
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
But why?

79
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I feel I should begin
by telling you about all that transpired

80
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
after you lost consciousness.

81
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Perhaps that way,
you'll better understand the outcome.

82
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Just as soon as you were out cold…

83
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Whenever he wakes up,

84
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
he'll probably decline his advancement.

85
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
He's right.
Sounds like something Gon would do.

86
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Only one person fails this round, right?

87
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
So, if Gon is disqualified,

88
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
then wouldn't that render
the rest of our upcoming fights

89
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,000
completely meaningless?

90
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
You've no need to worry.
Gon has certainly passed.

91
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Nothing he says or does
can change that now.

92
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[both sigh]

93
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Netero] As a matter of fact,

94
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
he could even throw a fit
and kill me where I stand,

95
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
but we still wouldn't be able
to revoke his license.

96
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Yes, I see.

97
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
So why?

98
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Why'd you let him win?

99
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
What did you say?

100
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
You didn't have to kill him.

101
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
With your skills,
you could've made him surrender...

102
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
somehow.

103
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
I expect, when I torture someone,

104
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
my victim will despise me
for the rest of their life.

105
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
It's more effective and less stressful.

106
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
When you're in pain,

107
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
your eyes show a gleam of hostility
toward the person responsible.

108
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Even with the most extensive
training and discipline,

109
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
that sign of rage
is difficult to suppress.

110
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
But Gon's eyes had no such gleam.

111
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Can you believe that?

112
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
I had just broken his arm.

113
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
But I could tell
just by looking into his eyes

114
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
that he had already forgotten
all about it.

115
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
So I guess you could say
the little guy won me over.

116
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Hmm.

117
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
If you need a reason why I "let him win,"
there you have it.

118
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
[Satotz] You won over your opponent, Gon.

119
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Hanzo admitted as much himself.

120
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
After that,
the second match of the Phase began.

121
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
[Masta] Round two! Kurapika versus Hisoka.

122
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Begin!

123
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Satotz] After the two of them
had been fighting for a while…

124
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
[grunts]

125
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[gasps]

126
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
[Hisoka chuckles]

127
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[Hisoka] I lose this one.

128
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
[Satotz] And that's how Kurapika won.

129
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[Gon] What did Hisoka say?

130
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
[Satotz] I couldn't say.

131
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
But I do know
that he conceded voluntarily.

132
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
The third match
pitted Hanzo against Pokkle.

133
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Pokkle found himself
In much the same position as you,

134
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
but he admitted defeat.
Almost immediately, in fact.

135
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
I'm sorry, but I won't go easy on you.

136
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[Satotz]
And with that, the match was over.

137
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
The fourth match was between
Hisoka and Bodoro.

138
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
[Bodoro yells]

139
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
[grunting]

140
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
[groans]

141
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
[Satotz]
The match was extremely one-sided,

142
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
but Bodoro flatly refused to give in.

143
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[groaning]

144
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
[Satotz] However,
while Bodoro was lying on the floor,

145
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Hisoka whispered something in his ear.

146
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
And this time, it was Bodoro
who surrendered.

147
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
The fifth match featured
Killua and Pokkle,

148
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
but Killua walked away
as soon as it began.

149
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
-[Pokkle] Huh?
-[Masta gasps]

150
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
In a confident tone, he declared…

151
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Yeah, sorry.

152
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
But I'm just not interested
in fighting you.

153
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
[Satotz] He must have felt certain
he could win his next match.

154
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
But then,

155
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Leorio requested
that the sixth match be postponed

156
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
while Bodoro recovered from his injuries.

157
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
So, in the meantime,

158
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
the match between Killua and Gitarrackur
was held.

159
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[Masta] Begin!

160
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
[Satotz] It became apparent that Killua
had made a grave miscalculation.

161
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
It's been a while, Kil.

162
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,000
[gasps]

163
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Big brother!

164
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:41,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

165
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:46,000
ILLUMI

166
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Wait. So Gitarrackur

167
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
is Killua's brother?

168
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Yes.

169
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
And his name is Illumi.

170
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[heavy breathing]

171
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Hey.

172
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
He's Killua's brother?

173
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Those needles were used
to change his appearance?

174
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
I heard you stabbed Mom and Milluki.

175
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Guess so.

176
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Mom couldn't stop crying.

177
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Well, who would blame her?

178
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Anybody'd cry if their kid did that.

179
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
She was just so happy.

180
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[Leorio gasps]

181
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:30,000
[Illumi] She was delighted to see
that her son had finally grown up.

182
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
But she's concerned about you
being out on your own.

183
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:38,000
And she asked me to check up on you
when I got the chance.

184
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Lucky me, huh?

185
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:44,000
I had absolutely no idea
that you wanted to be a Hunter.

186
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
As for me, I'm here to get a license
for a job that's coming up.

187
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
I don't actually want to become a Hunter.

188
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
I just felt like taking the Exam.

189
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
I see...

190
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Well, that's a relief.

191
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
In that case, I have some advice for you.

192
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
You're not cut out to be a Hunter.

193
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,000
You were born for one purpose:

194
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
To be an assassin.

195
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
That's really what he said?

196
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Killua mentioned his family,

197
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
but they sound crazy.

198
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
But that wasn't the extent of it.

199
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
You're a puppet of darkness,
devoid of passion.

200
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:40,000
There is nothing you desire,
nor is there anything you wish for.

201
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
As one who lives in the shadows,

202
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
the only pleasure you're capable of
is derived from causing death.

203
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Because that's how Dad and I raised you.

204
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
What do you imagine
that you would accomplish

205
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
by becoming a Hunter?

206
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Killua] It's true.

207
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
I don't really want to be a Hunter.

208
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
But...

209
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
everyone wants something.

210
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Even me.

211
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
-[Illumi] You don't.
-Wrong!

212
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
There is something that I really want!

213
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[Illumi] Hmm...

214
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Enlighten me. What is it that you want?

215
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Hmm...

216
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
What's the matter?

217
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
There really isn't anything, is there?

218
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
There is!

219
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I...

220
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
want to be...

221
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
friends with Gon.

222
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,000
I'm... I'm just so sick of killing people.

223
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
I want to be friends with Gon...

224
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,000
and just have fun.

225
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Impossible.

226
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
You are incapable of friendship.

227
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
The only thing that you can do

228
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,000
is discern whether or not
you can kill them.

229
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
That is all you were ever taught.

230
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Gon is such a radiant personality
that you don't know how to classify him.

231
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
You don't actually desire his friendship.

232
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
No…

233
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
[Illumi] If you stay with him,

234
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
one day you'll end up
wanting to kill him.

235
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
You'll wonder if you can.

236
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
And you'll want to find out.

237
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Because…

238
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
you are, by nature, a murderer.

239
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
[shuddering breaths]

240
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[grumbles]

241
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
We've warned you already, sir.

242
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
-So please…
-[Leorio] Yeah, yeah, I know.

243
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[shouting] Killua!

244
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
I couldn't care less
if this guy's your brother, all right?

245
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
He's a worthless piece of crap!

246
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
So don't listen to him!

247
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Just beat the crap out of him like usual
and win!

248
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
You want to become friends with Gon?

249
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Are you kiddin' me?

250
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
You're already friends!
How do you not know that?

251
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
-[Killua gasps]
-[Illumi] Huh?

252
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[Leorio]
Gon sure seems to think so, anyway!

253
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Is that true?

254
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Hell yeah, it's true, you idiot!

255
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Oh, no. That isn't good.

256
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
So he already considers Kil a friend?

257
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Fine. Then I'll just kill Gon!

258
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
[all gasp]

259
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
[Illumi]
Assassins have no use for friends.

260
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
They only get in the way.

261
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
[shuddering breaths]

262
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Where can I find him?

263
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
[examiner] Please, wait a second!
The match is still--

264
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[groans]

265
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[painful gurgling]

266
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
-[Illumi] Where?
-[examiner groans]

267
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[strained]
He's in the waiting room right over there…

268
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
-[Illumi] Thank you.
-[groaning in pain]

269
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Hmm?

270
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Oh, what a pain.

271
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I need to acquire a Hunter's license
right now

272
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
so I can do my job.

273
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
But if I kill them, I'll fail,

274
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
and then Kil will pass automatically.

275
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Oh, no!

276
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
The same thing will happen
if I kill Gon.

277
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Hmm... Wait!

278
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[chuckling]
I'll pass the Exam and then kill Gon!

279
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[shuddering breaths]

280
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,000
You bastard!

281
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
[Illumi] If I pass the Exam first,

282
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,000
I can kill everyone here
and still keep my license,

283
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,000
isn't that right?

284
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Well... yes, according to the rulebook.

285
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[Illumi] Did you hear that, Kil?

286
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:46,000
If you really want to save Gon,
you're going to have to beat me.

287
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Will you fight me to save your friend?

288
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
You can't do it, can you?

289
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Because deep down,

290
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:02,000
you're more worried about whether
you can defeat me than anything else,

291
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
aren't you?

292
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
[gasps]

293
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
[Illumi]
And... you already know the answer.

294
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,000
"I'm not strong enough
to beat my big brother."

295
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Remember the lesson I drilled into you?

296
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Never go up against a superior opponent.

297
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[panicked breathing]

298
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[Illumi] Don't move!

299
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Move one more inch,
and I'll assume the fight has begun.

300
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:33,000
The same goes for if our bodies
come in contact with each other.

301
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,000
The fight starts.

302
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
There is only one way to stop me,

303
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
and you know it.

304
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
But don't forget...

305
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
If you decide that you won't fight me,

306
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
your dear Gon will certainly die.

307
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Take him out, Killua!

308
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
We'll protect you!
He won't kill you or Gon!

309
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
We'll do whatever we have to do
to stop him!

310
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Go on! Let him have it!

311
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
[shuddering breath]

312
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[Killua] You win, Illumi.

313
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
I admit defeat.

314
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
[Kurapika and Leorio gasping]

315
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Oh! Excellent!

316
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
No need for us to fight then, huh?

317
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,000
[laughs]

318
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,000
I lied, Kil.

319
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
I was never going to kill Gon.

320
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
That was only a test
to see what you were made of.

321
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
And now I know for certain.

322
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
You are simply not qualified
to make friends.

323
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Not that you need any.

324
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
You'll keep doing what you've always done:

325
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
the job Dad and I trained you to do.

326
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
I'll order you to take the Hunter Exam
when the time is right.

327
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
But not now.

328
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
[Satotz]
Something drained out of Killua then.

329
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Leorio and Kurapika
did their best to help,

330
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
but he simply wouldn't respond.

331
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:12,000
The sixth match
was between Leorio and Bodoro.

332
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Bodoro had recovered,
but at the onset of the match…

333
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,000
[Masta] Begin!

334
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
[Satotz] It was over in a flash.

335
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:49,000
And so, just like that,
Killua killed Bodoro.

336
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:53,000
The committee disqualified him,
though that goes without saying.

337
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
-[Satotz] Gon!
-[Gon] Where is everybody?

338
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[Satotz] You must lie down!
You need to rest!

339
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
[footsteps approaching]

340
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Gon!

341
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Apologize to Killua!

342
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,000
[narrator] Gon was angry.

343
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Illumi had trampled on Killua's desire
to be Gon's friend,

344
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
sending his younger brother
into deep despair.

345
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
In fact, Gon was more than angry.

346
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
He was furious.

347
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[theme song playing]

348
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Next time: Some Brother Trouble!

349
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Do Leorio and I look alike?

350
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Get outta here…
